{
  "rationale": "Use a small plant split into sensing and motion capability, then encode the exploration/recovery policy in specifications. The policy gives one controllable action per active decision/recovery state, keeps all uncontrollable events defined at every state, treats obstacle events as safety-critical preemptions in action states, prefers forward progress in clear conditions, uses brief directed turns for side/front obstacles, uses move_backward only in dedicated front-recovery states, and reserves full_rotate for a dedicated repeated-failure last-resort path.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate sensor outcomes and motion capabilities into plant automata so specifications can enforce safe action selection.",
    "Use one main policy specification plus a small progress-bias specification to prefer move_forward over random_walk in clear conditions while still allowing random_walk after repeated front blockage."
  ],
